    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488-a3">

                <pb facs="0453" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg379"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>The Minister of Sweden and Norway to
                        Mr. Clay</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St. Petersburg,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 16-28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency:</hi> In hastening to acknowledge the
                    sad communication by which your excellency has just informed me of the
                    assassination of Mr. Lincoln, President of the United States of America, I beg
                    you to accept my most profound expressions of sympathy, and also, of horror for
                    the foul deed which has deprived your country and your government of their
                    worthy and illustrious chief.</p>
                <p>I seize the present occasion to offer to your excellency repeated assurances of
                    my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WEDEL YARLSBERG, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Sweden and
                            Norway.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. C. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clay</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Minister of the United States of America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
